    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-04T09:31:48+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-04T09:31:48+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-03T23:01:48Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-03T23:01:48Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough over the northwest will weaken today with a high pressure ridge south of the state expected to move north and hover over SA during Monday. A cold front is forecast to pass over the southeast early Tuesday, then quickly followed by a high pressure system that is expected to pass to the south of the state later Tuesday and on Wednesday, maintaining a ridge over the state.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-05T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-04T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. High chance of showers, becoming less likely in the late afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Coober Pedy. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures between 19 and 24.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:40am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-05T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-06T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-04T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-05T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog in the far west. Light winds becoming south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late afternoon then tending south to southeasterly in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-06T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-07T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-05T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-06T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. The chance of morning fog south of Coober Pedy. Light winds becoming southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-07T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-08T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-06T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-07T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
